<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Exact Values of Sine, Cosine, and Tangent Without a Calculator</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Without using a calculator, write down the exact values of the following. Use e.g. <tt>sqrt(2)</tt> for \(\sqrt{2}\).</p>
<ol type="a">
<li><div>\(\sin {@A1@}^{\circ} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div></li>
<li><div>\(\sin {@A2@}^{\circ} = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div></li>
<li><div>\(\cos {@A1@}^{\circ} = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div></li>
<li><div>\(\cos {@A2@}^{\circ} = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div></li>
<li><div>\(\tan {@A1@}^{\circ} = \) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</div></li>
<li><div>\(\tan {@A2@}^{\circ} = \) [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]]</div></li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Both angles are obtuse, so they lie in the second quadrant, where sine is positive while cosine and tangent are negative. Each exact value follows from the reference (supplementary) angle \(180^\circ - \theta\), which is one of the standard angles \(30^\circ\), \(45^\circ\) or \(60^\circ\):</p>
<ol type="a">
<li>\( \sin {@A1@}^\circ = \sin(180^\circ - {@A1@}^\circ) = \sin {@ref1@}^\circ = {@ta1@} \)</li>
<li>\( \sin {@A2@}^\circ = \sin(180^\circ - {@A2@}^\circ) = \sin {@ref2@}^\circ = {@ta2@} \)</li>
<li>\( \cos {@A1@}^\circ = -\cos {@ref1@}^\circ = {@ta3@} \)</li>
<li>\( \cos {@A2@}^\circ = -\cos {@ref2@}^\circ = {@ta4@} \)</li>
<li>\( \tan {@A1@}^\circ = \dfrac{\sin {@A1@}^\circ}{\cos {@A1@}^\circ} = {@ta5@} \)</li>
<li>\( \tan {@A2@}^\circ = \dfrac{\sin {@A2@}^\circ}{\cos {@A2@}^\circ} = {@ta6@} \)</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>6</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
